    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (23 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\n`membershipNumber` is a **derived field** \u2014 computed from the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, matching the existing `displayName`/`initials` pattern (which are also mapper expressions, not stored columns). So no entity or DB changes were needed.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `membershipNumber` string property to the `Owner` schema (this generates the `membershipNumber` field/getter on `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   `year % 100` with `%02d` yields the zero-padded last two digits (e.g. 2026 \u2192 `26`, 2007 \u2192 `07`), producing `SMI-0007-M26`.\n\n`registrationDate` is always populated (`BuildOwner` defaults it to today if omitted) and `customerCode` is always assigned earlier in the POST pipeline, so the expression is safe. `Cp14Tests.coreMembershipNumberFormat` passes and no existing tests regressed.",
